WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.834
WATAM DeFi Intelligence turns on-chain swap
data into findings your team can verify.

00:00:07.294 --> 00:00:11.591
In the next few minutes, we'll walk through
the workflow: verified data, a token

00:00:11.631 --> 00:00:14.952
report, an anomaly finding with its
evidence, and the analyst.

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:20.821
When a token's trading activity suddenly
jumps, the first question is simple: what

00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:23.525
actually happened, and can we trust the
numbers?

00:00:23.985 --> 00:00:28.568
Every view in the platform answers with
evidence you can check, not with a black box.

00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:31.159
Start on the Data platform.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:36.137
Swap events are collected from public RPC
endpoints for historical windows.

00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:41.459
A run is published only when its coverage,
decoding, time-window and uniqueness

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:44.561
gates pass. If a gate fails, nothing is
published.

00:00:45.021 --> 00:00:50.409
Below, the token table lists every token
with verified pool-swap data, its network,

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.240
contract and covered window.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.503
Select a token to open its report.

00:00:55.963 --> 00:01:03.293
For ARB on Arbitrum One, the window has 68
verified covered hours and 64,763 pool

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:06.842
swap events across four selected pools.

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:12.419
The chart splits buys and sells by hour, and the
pool table shows where the activity happened.

00:01:12.879 --> 00:01:17.652
The report also states what it does not
cover: these are the selected pools only,

00:01:17.692 --> 00:01:19.732
and pool events are not net trades.

00:01:21.022 --> 00:01:27.078
To look at another token, the Token explorer verifies
the contract on-chain and discovers its pools.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.601
Each pool is checked against a supported
protocol family, so unsupported venues are

00:01:32.641 --> 00:01:35.552
listed openly instead of being silently
dropped.

00:01:36.842 --> 00:01:41.878
Next, the Anomaly center. Filter by network
and severity, and each finding appears

00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:45.469
with its window and the observed value
against a baseline.

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:53.345
For VELO on OP Mainnet, swap activity
reached 12.8× its frozen baseline, and token

00:01:53.385 --> 00:01:58.164
volume reached 7.43× and 7.25× in two
separate hours.

00:01:59.454 --> 00:02:04.493
Open a finding to see exactly how it was
measured: the method and its parameters,

00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:08.695
the frozen baseline, alternative
explanations and follow-up checks.

00:02:09.155 --> 00:02:14.968
Show SQL evidence reveals the query behind the
series, so an analyst can reproduce the number.

00:02:15.428 --> 00:02:20.889
A finding is a statistical observation. It
does not establish intent or manipulation.

00:02:22.179 --> 00:02:25.472
To compare two periods, choose a reference
window and compare.

00:02:25.932 --> 00:02:30.313
A change counts as comparable only when
every pool is covered in both windows.

00:02:30.773 --> 00:02:35.246
Here the pool set differs, so the platform
marks the comparison as incomplete,

00:02:35.286 --> 00:02:37.502
instead of showing a misleading change.

00:02:38.792 --> 00:02:42.066
Finally, ask the Conversational analyst in
plain language.

00:02:42.526 --> 00:02:47.485
Answers are built only from verified facts,
and every number must match a cited fact.

00:02:47.945 --> 00:02:52.695
If no model can serve, or a sentence doesn't
check out, you get a clearly labelled

00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:55.090
deterministic answer from the same facts.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:00.873
Local models are used by default. Nothing is
sent to a cloud service unless you approve it.

00:03:02.163 --> 00:03:07.376
WATAM DeFi Intelligence is self-hosted,
works on historical ingested windows, and

00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:09.775
states exactly which pools it covers.

00:03:10.235 --> 00:03:14.456
To see it on your own tokens, scope a
private pilot with us at

00:03:14.496 --> 00:03:16.381
admin@wearetheartmakers.com.
